<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="361f233c">&lt;p&gt;
    Describes how the system will be configured and what will be included in the standard system configuration. It is a
    baseline that captures the detailed configuration requirements and defines the configuration strategy including tools,
    deployment procedures and documentation standards. A baseline allows changes to the configuration to be tracked and the
    changes can be compared to this baseline. It acts as a basis for change control that can be referenced later in the
    project.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="cabe1e4c"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="1a315b68"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="eafeb7eb"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="c39fe5e9">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose is to:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define configuration specifications needed to develop a “custom” configuration that meets the unique requirements
        of the client
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define the characteristics that need to be achieved by the package solution&apos;s configuration
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="76dcc67d">Without this baseline configuration, changes to the configuration cannot be tracked or analyzed. In addition, the
technical team would not know when to begin the configuration activities.</attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="3d305d72"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="42552f3a">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product includes:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Functionality design that defines how: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                To achieve &quot;out of the box&quot; functionality
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Sets of business activities must be executed or rolled back as one unit
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Orchestration of multiple functions are performed to complete the end-to-end service to a customer
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                General parameters and the settings govern the behavior of the package
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        User interface design that defines how: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                New and modified screens work together in the application to help the user reach a particular goal
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Detailed fields, buttons and other user interface elements are required to perform a task on a screen
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                The structure of the regular or ad-hoc reports are generated by the package
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                The structure of the forms used with the package
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Security design that defines how: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Authentication, authorization, and security reporting are defined
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Operations design that defines how: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Batch programs are required by the package to operate
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Automated Job Control Language (JCL) scripting language is needed to run the batch processes in the proper
                sequence
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Configuration rationale: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Describes why a configuration setting has been defined in a particular way.
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Provides an explanation of why the system was configured with specific values or settings for future
                reference of the stakeholder
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Limitations and dependencies&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
